# Documentation Rules

## Module learnings
- When you discover something non-obvious about how a module works (a gotcha,
  an undocumented assumption, a design tradeoff, a bug pattern), append a
  dated entry to `docs/notes/<module-name>.md`.
- Do NOT create a new notes file per source file — one file per top-level
  src/ module.
- Keep entries factual and terse. No entry for things a comment already
  explains clearly.

## Feature domain notes
- All feature domain notes live in `docs/notes/features.md`, one
  `## <domain>` section per folder under `src/features/`.
- Split a domain out into its own `docs/notes/features-<domain>.md` when
  ANY of the following is true:
  - Its section reaches ~8-10 dated entries
  - It involves external integrations, payments, or auth/compliance concerns
    (split proactively even with few entries)
  - You're told explicitly to split it
- When splitting: move existing entries, replace the section in features.md
  with a one-line pointer, and update the link in LEARNINGS.md.

## Changelog
- After making a code change (new feature, bug fix, refactor, breaking
  change), add an entry under `## [Unreleased]` in `CHANGELOG.md`,
  categorized as Added / Changed / Fixed / Removed.
- Never edit past dated release entries in the changelog.
- Do not add changelog entries for trivial changes (formatting, typo fixes,
  comments) unless asked.
